# playpick gave mode=battleground map=flags spec=warrior:arms style=flee
# view=844x390,touch save=carried. Checked against the ledger and every
# .play under playtest/plans/ before committing: warrior:arms has been
# played in mode=daily and in mode=raid before, but never once on a
# battleground (the eleven prior battleground sessions cover druid x4,
# shaman x3, hunter, mage, paladin, priest x2, warlock -- no warrior). And
# the only prior flee+flags pull on record (2026-09-27, mage:frost, same
# view) found a *ranged* class wandering onto Ebb and Flow's dropped flag,
# becoming its carrier by proximity alone (no press involved), and dying to
# CARRIER_FRAGILITY with no way to fight back -- flee's steering has no
# notion of carrying or dropping a flag. This pull swaps in a melee class to
# see whether that is a flag-map property or a ranged-class property: arms
# has a shorter attack range than frost, so if flee still drifts it onto the
# flag the same way, the carrier death is the map's, not the spec's. #278
# already covers Ebb and Flow's real 180s limit vs README's claimed 360s, so
# the chunks below sum past 180s on purpose to watch the match actually end.
open
targets
shot front

tap battleground
tap map:flags
targets
shot flags-picked

tap class:warrior:arms
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot pulled
state
targets

play flee 60
shot mid1
state
bill
says

wait 5
play flee 60
shot mid2
state
bill

wait 5
play flee 70
shot mid3
state
bill
says
targets
